      "id": "hackernews-2026-05-14-show-hn-gridtravel-a-community-based-travel-app-for-users-to",
      "title": "Show HN: GridTravel- A community based travel app for users to share routes",
      "summary": "Hey HN,\nMy co-founders and I have been building GridTravel, a free iOS app for planning and sharing travel routes with turn-by-turn GPS nav. We just launched yesterday after App Store approval.\nWe're three 21-year-old cofounders and best friends since middle school. We built GridTravel after years of frustration navigating new cities on every trip we took together.\nThe idea: most people either sea",
      "body": "Discover citieslike a local.Walking routes built by people who actually live there — with the tips you'd only know if you knew someone. Turn-by-turn, offline-ready, made for travelers.Share your routes. Walk theirs.GridTravel turns the walks people take every day into turn-by-turn navigation for travelers everywhere — with the tips you'd only know if you were a local.Your profile, your progress.Every walk you take, every route you save — collected into a quietly beautiful overview of your travel life.Personal OverviewYour profile, routes, and essentials — gathered in one calm, focused view.Activity InsightsTrack saved routes, downloads, and progress — in real time, on every walk.Performance StatsDistance, cities explored, and routes conquered — the receipts for every adventure.A map full of secrets.Trending spots and quiet corners, all on one interactive map. Filter by mood, follow the locals you love, and find the walk that fits the day.Map & list, side by sideBrowse visually or scan the list — pick the lens that fits how you're hunting.Follow your favorite localsSubscribe to creators whose taste matches yours and see their new routes first.Made for the way you wanderFoodie, scenic, historical, nightlife — filter and find the route that fits your mood today.Every stop, in advance.Preview every stop on a route — the photos, the tips, the timing. Download for offline, save for later, or just start walking.From map to memory, in four steps.A walking experience tuned for the way people actually move through a city — clear, calm, and never in your way.1Pick a routeBrowse local walks by vibe — foodie, scenic, historical, hidden.2Preview every stopSee each location, photo, and insider tip before you commit.3Walk turn-by-turnOptimized for sidewalks — clear cues, never a wrong turn.4Save & shareBookmark walks for later or share favorites with a friend.More than a guidebook.Real routes, real tips, real travelers — built for the way people actually walk a city.Real routes from real peopleEvery walk is made by a local who actually took it — no algorithm-generated tourist traps. Just paths someone would lead a friend down.Built for walkersTurn-by-turn cues tuned for sidewalks — not highways or commutes.Insider tipsThe best photo angle. The secret menu item. The local story.Works offline, wherever you wanderDownload routes ahead of time and walk confidently — no signal, no problem.Download GridTravel.Walk the world.A community of locals making the walks they take their friends on. Find a route. Start walking.",
