      "summary": "A growing number of Labour MPs are coming out against the prime minister.",
      "body": "PA MediaA growing number of Labour MPs are coming out against Prime Minister Sir Keir Starmer, with some calling for him to resign and others urging him to set out a timetable for his departure.Four ministers, including Safeguarding Minister Jess Phillips, have resigned.Labour's process for removing a leader requires 81 MPs to back a single challenger. Although there are more than 80 calling for the prime minister's resignation, there is currently no unified support for one specific opponent.Meanwhile separately, more than 100 backbenchers and junior ministers have signed a statement saying this is \"no time for a leadership contest\".Which ministers have resigned?Jess Phillips, safeguarding ministerZubir Ahmed, health ministerAlex Davies-Jones, victims ministerMiatta Fahnbulleh, minister for devolution, faith and communitiesWhich Labour MPs have criticised Starmer's leadership?Debbie Abrahams - MP for Oldham East & SaddleworthZubir Ahmed - MP for Glasgow South WestTahir Ali - MP for Birmingham Hall Green & MoseleyTonia Antoniazzi – MP for Gower James Asser - MP for West Ham & Beckton Jas Athwal - MP for Ilford SouthDavid Baines - MP for St Helens North Richard Baker - MP for Glenrothes & Mid Fife Alex Ballinger – MP for HalesowenPaula Barker- MP for  Liverpool WavertreeLorraine Beavers- MP for Blackpool North & FleetwoodApsana Begum - MP for Poplar & LimehouseClive Betts - MP for Sheffield South EastMatt Bishop - MP for Forest of DeanOlivia Blake - MP for Sheffield HallamJonathan Brash – MP for HartlepoolRichard Burgon - MP for Leeds EastMaureen Burke - MP for Glasgow North EastIan Byrne- MP for Liverpool West DerbyMarkus Campbell-Savours - MP for Penrith & SolwayIrene Campbell - MP for Ayrshire North & ArranSam Carling - MP for Cambridgeshire North WestLizzi Collinge - MP for Morecambe and LunesdaleAndrew Cooper - MP for Mid CheshireBeccy Cooper - MP for Worthing WestJen Craft - MP for ThurrockChris Curtis - MP for Milton Keynes NorthPaul Davies - M