      "id": "bbc-2026-05-05-tech-life",
      "title": "Tech Life",
      "summary": "A sleep apnoea wearable. Plus, tech to free up hospital beds and a breast health app.",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsWorld Service,·05 May 2026,·26 minsCould this tech help millions of us sleep better?Tech LifeAvailable for over a yearAn anti-snoring device is being trialled as a potential solution to sleep apnoea, a condition which affects millions and can have wide-ranging consequences on daily life. We speak to the team behind the trial.\nAlso on the programme, two health tech entrepreneurs whose personal experiences informed their products: A man who had a heart attack at 44 and now works to help reduce hospital recovery times, and a woman who lost a close family member to breast cancer and is working to help inform women in Pakistan to spot the signs and get help.\nProducers: Tom Quinn and Imran Rahman-Jones\n(Image: A man asleep in bed with a black boomerang-shaped device attached to his neck. Credit: Zeus Sleeps)Programme WebsiteMore episodes",
